                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "233546992",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198063465895",
                            "num_reviews": 694,
                            "playtime_forever": 414,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 414,
                            "last_played": 1787520183
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Empire of the Gods is a decently fun strategy card game with an interesting theme (though it's quite shallow) and a competent gameplay loop. While I didn't find myself going \"oh wow, i wish this was over\", I also didn't have any moments that stuck out as bad or poorly designed. It works well, has no bugs, glitches, issues, artifacting or really anything wrong with it whatsoever - and does it's job competently and well. That's really as far as I can go, as while I'm a big fan of the setting and I can't find any fault with what was actually made, there wasn't enough of a hook to make me *eager* to keep playing. I think I might've stopped early if I wasn't a completionist, but that might just be because this game is ultimately quite simple.\r\n\r\nAll in All, though, it does exactly what it sets out to do and does it well and without complaint. That's somewhat rare in my experience, so I'll give it praise for that. Nicely done, Empire of the Gods.",
